{"id": "EUVD-2026-81808", "enisaUuid": "1b8abb2f-40ff-36e7-93d5-6c470c3977a6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: ubi: Release device reference on busy detach\n\nubi_detach_mtd_dev() obtains a device reference through ubi_get_device()\nbefore checking whether the UBI device is busy. The busy return path drops\nubi->ref_count but leaves the device reference held, so the device object\ncannot be released after a later detach.\n\nDrop the device reference before returning -EBUSY.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87812858c4c8df979cb70bcd0040b925a543df6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e065960366b55ab21e6c643c30dec2a41451900b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/851c5e9a829d56cb0982965f07ef8966a6722884", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31dd710cd84d5dd63c49f640d3a9f36c9699ca95"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90215", "GHSA-387j-r42m-fpjv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "107fe7ff-d528-3baa-8fda-6f7354ec6612", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "118713cb-9ef0-30bb-82ad-09c03184fd65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7e84c961b2eb062d2f47037dcca52dcd1d3615b5 <851c5e9a829d56cb0982965f07ef8966a6722884"}, {"id": "18cc311b-062c-3e31-b8e4-0fc395aadc7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7e84c961b2eb062d2f47037dcca52dcd1d3615b5 <31dd710cd84d5dd63c49f640d3a9f36c9699ca95"}, {"id": "66e91a45-cf89-3770-ba48-3b07ace2fb2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "67fc6677-63e9-3c12-a025-599bb076267a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7e84c961b2eb062d2f47037dcca52dcd1d3615b5 <87812858c4c8df979cb70bcd0040b925a543df6f"}, {"id": "b0d0